From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 09:33:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/62] verimark: BULK async transceive for the IT handshake
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first IT runtime open() returned VERIMARK_HANDSHAKE_ERR_READ
(-3) because the async orchestrator was routing both TX1
(ClientHello -> ServerHello) and TX2 (Flight2 -> Server CCS +
encrypted Finished) through verimark_transceive_async, which is
hard-wired to vendor CONTROL transfers (bRequest 0x16 / 0x17
DT-only). The IT speaks the same Tudor TLS family but over BULK
endpoints (EP01 OUT, EP81 IN) — control transfers on the IT
return nothing, the read side times out, hence -3.

Adds verimark_transceive_async_bulk in transport.{h,c}, sharing
the existing VerimarkTransceiveAsyncCtx and verimark_transceive_
finish so the orchestrator just dispatches on is_it_variant:

    if (ctx->is_it_variant) {
        verimark_transceive_async_bulk(...);
    } else {
        verimark_transceive_async(...);
    }

Done at both TX1 and TX2 sites in handshake.c. The IT path drops
the 8-byte alignment and the wValue-from-length trick that only
apply to the DT's vendor control framing.

Buffers carry the 4-byte 44 00 00 00 transport prefix on
handshake records (already prepended in handshake_async_build_
client_hello and the flight2 builder) — no change needed there.

Response buffers are 256 bytes, plenty for the IT's known reply
sizes (66 B ServerHello + CertReq + ServerHelloDone ; 51 B
ServerCCS + encrypted Finished). The single bulk_transfer_async
IN call returns once the firmware sends a short packet (< 64 B),
which all IT handshake replies do — same termination semantics
the Python harness uses, runtime-validated 2026-06-07.

verimark_bulk_in already mirrors the Python bulk_read_all multi-
chunk loop for the sync path used by verimark_it_reset_session ;
the async transceive is one bulk_out + one bulk_in, which is
sufficient for the handshake TXs.

12 standalone tests still green. Full libfprint build clean.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/handshake.c |  55 +++++++++----
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c | 108 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.h |  18 +++++
 3 files changed, 165 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/handshake.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/handshake.c
index cd591fa..f56b140 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/handshake.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/handshake.c
@@ -907,14 +907,25 @@ handshake_async_tx1_done(GObject *obj, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
         return;
     }
 
-    /* Kick off TX2 : send flight2, read server response. */
-    verimark_transceive_async(ctx->transport,
-                              ctx->wire_flight, ctx->wire_flight_len,
-                              ctx->bufs->server_response,
-                              sizeof(ctx->bufs->server_response),
-                              ctx->timeout_ms,
-                              ctx->cancellable,
-                              handshake_async_tx2_done, task);
+    /* Kick off TX2 : send flight2, read server response. Same DT/IT
+     * dispatch as TX1. */
+    if (ctx->is_it_variant) {
+        verimark_transceive_async_bulk(ctx->transport,
+                                        ctx->wire_flight, ctx->wire_flight_len,
+                                        ctx->bufs->server_response,
+                                        sizeof(ctx->bufs->server_response),
+                                        ctx->timeout_ms,
+                                        ctx->cancellable,
+                                        handshake_async_tx2_done, task);
+    } else {
+        verimark_transceive_async(ctx->transport,
+                                  ctx->wire_flight, ctx->wire_flight_len,
+                                  ctx->bufs->server_response,
+                                  sizeof(ctx->bufs->server_response),
+                                  ctx->timeout_ms,
+                                  ctx->cancellable,
+                                  handshake_async_tx2_done, task);
+    }
 }
 
 
@@ -969,14 +980,26 @@ verimark_handshake_perform_async(
         return;
     }
 
-    /* Kick off TX1 : send ClientHello, read ServerHello. */
-    verimark_transceive_async(transport,
-                              ctx->wire_ch, ctx->wire_ch_len,
-                              ctx->bufs->sh_record,
-                              sizeof(ctx->bufs->sh_record),
-                              timeout_ms,
-                              cancellable,
-                              handshake_async_tx1_done, task);
+    /* Kick off TX1 : send ClientHello, read ServerHello.
+     * IT uses BULK on EP01/EP81 ; DT uses vendor control transfers
+     * (0x16 / 0x17). Both async helpers share the same finish API. */
+    if (ctx->is_it_variant) {
+        verimark_transceive_async_bulk(transport,
+                                        ctx->wire_ch, ctx->wire_ch_len,
+                                        ctx->bufs->sh_record,
+                                        sizeof(ctx->bufs->sh_record),
+                                        timeout_ms,
+                                        cancellable,
+                                        handshake_async_tx1_done, task);
+    } else {
+        verimark_transceive_async(transport,
+                                  ctx->wire_ch, ctx->wire_ch_len,
+                                  ctx->bufs->sh_record,
+                                  sizeof(ctx->bufs->sh_record),
+                                  timeout_ms,
+                                  cancellable,
+                                  handshake_async_tx1_done, task);
+    }
 }
 
 
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
index 0991a9f..8340341 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
@@ -528,6 +528,114 @@ verimark_transceive_async(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
 }
 
 
+/* --- transceive_async_bulk : OUT EP01 then IN EP81 (IT) ------------- */
+
+static void
+verimark_transceive_bulk_in_cb(GObject *obj, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
+{
+    GTask *task = G_TASK(ud);
+    VerimarkTransceiveAsyncCtx *ctx = g_task_get_task_data(task);
+    GError *err = NULL;
+    /* libgusb returns the byte count via gssize, mirroring the
+     * synchronous bulk_transfer's `actual_length` out parameter. */
+    gssize n = g_usb_device_bulk_transfer_finish(G_USB_DEVICE(obj),
+                                                  res, &err);
+    if (n < 0) {
+        if (err == NULL)
+            err = g_error_new(G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_FAILED,
+                              "transceive_bulk: IN failed");
+        g_task_return_error(task, err);
+        g_object_unref(task);
+        return;
+    }
+    ctx->resp_len = (size_t)n;
+    g_task_return_boolean(task, TRUE);
+    g_object_unref(task);
+}
+
+
+static void
+verimark_transceive_bulk_out_cb(GObject *obj, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
+{
+    GTask *task = G_TASK(ud);
+    VerimarkTransceiveAsyncCtx *ctx = g_task_get_task_data(task);
+    GError *err = NULL;
+    gssize n = g_usb_device_bulk_transfer_finish(G_USB_DEVICE(obj),
+                                                  res, &err);
+    if (n < 0) {
+        if (err == NULL)
+            err = g_error_new(G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_FAILED,
+                              "transceive_bulk: OUT failed");
+        g_task_return_error(task, err);
+        g_object_unref(task);
+        return;
+    }
+    if ((size_t)n != ctx->send_aligned) {
+        g_task_return_new_error(task, G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_FAILED,
+                                "transceive_bulk: OUT short write %zd / %zu",
+                                n, ctx->send_aligned);
+        g_object_unref(task);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    /* Chain the IN on EP81. The firmware terminates handshake responses
+     * with a short packet (< 64 B), so libusb returns once the full
+     * record has been read into resp. */
+    GUsbDevice *dev = (GUsbDevice *)ctx->h->native;
+    g_usb_device_bulk_transfer_async(
+        dev,
+        VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_IN,
+        ctx->resp, ctx->resp_size,
+        ctx->timeout_ms,
+        ctx->cancellable,
+        verimark_transceive_bulk_in_cb, task);
+}
+
+
+void
+verimark_transceive_async_bulk(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
+                                const uint8_t *data,
+                                size_t data_len,
+                                uint8_t *resp,
+                                size_t resp_size,
+                                unsigned timeout_ms,
+                                GCancellable *cancellable,
+                                GAsyncReadyCallback callback,
+                                gpointer user_data)
+{
+    GTask *task = g_task_new(NULL, cancellable, callback, user_data);
+    g_task_set_source_tag(task, verimark_transceive_async_bulk);
+
+    if (h == NULL || data == NULL || data_len == 0 || resp == NULL) {
+        g_task_return_new_error(task, G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT,
+                                "transceive_async_bulk: invalid arg");
+        g_object_unref(task);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    VerimarkTransceiveAsyncCtx *ctx = g_new0(VerimarkTransceiveAsyncCtx, 1);
+    ctx->h = h;
+    ctx->resp = resp;
+    ctx->resp_size = resp_size;
+    ctx->timeout_ms = timeout_ms;
+    ctx->cancellable = cancellable;
+    /* BULK has no alignment / wValue quirks — copy `data` as-is. */
+    ctx->send_buf = g_malloc(data_len);
+    memcpy(ctx->send_buf, data, data_len);
+    ctx->send_aligned = data_len;
+    g_task_set_task_data(task, ctx, verimark_transceive_async_ctx_free);
+
+    GUsbDevice *dev = (GUsbDevice *)h->native;
+    g_usb_device_bulk_transfer_async(
+        dev,
+        VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_OUT,
+        ctx->send_buf, data_len,
+        timeout_ms,
+        cancellable,
+        verimark_transceive_bulk_out_cb, task);
+}
+
+
 VerimarkResult
 verimark_transceive_finish(GAsyncResult *res, size_t *out_resp_len,
                           GError **error)
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.h b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.h
index fe8c6c8..4d5af2c 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.h
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.h
@@ -360,6 +360,24 @@ void verimark_transceive_async(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
                                GAsyncReadyCallback callback,
                                gpointer user_data);
 
+/**
+ * BULK variant of `verimark_transceive_async` for the IT (047d:8054) :
+ * writes `data` to EP01 OUT then reads the response on EP81 IN. No
+ * wValue / 8-byte alignment quirks (those are DT control-transfer
+ * specifics). Completion semantics and finish API are identical to
+ * `verimark_transceive_async` — the same `verimark_transceive_finish`
+ * is used to retrieve the actual byte count.
+ */
+void verimark_transceive_async_bulk(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
+                                     const uint8_t *data,
+                                     size_t data_len,
+                                     uint8_t *resp,
+                                     size_t resp_size,
+                                     unsigned timeout_ms,
+                                     GCancellable *cancellable,
+                                     GAsyncReadyCallback callback,
+                                     gpointer user_data);
+
 VerimarkResult verimark_transceive_finish(GAsyncResult *res,
                                           size_t *out_resp_len,
                                           GError **error);
